{title: Dwell in the House}
{subtitle: Psalms 27:4}
{key: Bb}
{tempo: 75}
{time: 6/8}

{comment: Intro}
| [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] | [Bb] |
| [Bb] |

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
The Lord is my light and my salvation
[Gm7]I have no reason to fear
[Eb]He is the stronghold of my life
My [Bb/F]heart will not be af[Fsus4]raid
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[Bb]Evildoers close in to devour me
[Gm7]But they will stumble and fall
[Eb]Though an army camps against me
My [Fsus4]confidence stands [F]tall
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
One thing I [Bb]ask of the Lord
This is the [Gm7]only thing I seek
To dwell in the [Eb]house of the Lord
For all the [Bb/F]days that I [F]have
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[Bb]I want to gaze on his beauty
And [Gm7]seek him in his temple
In [Eb]the day of trouble he keeps me
[Fsus4]Safe in his shel[F]ter
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
[Eb]He hides me under [Gm7]the cover
Of [Bb]his tent upon a [F]rock
[Eb]My head is lift[Gm7]ed high above
The [Bb]enemies who sur[F]round me
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I will [Eb]sing and make [Gm]music
To the [Bb]Lord in his [F]tent
Hear [Eb]my voice when [Gm]I call
Be [Bb]gracious and answer [F]me
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
One thing I [Bb]ask of the Lord
This is the [Gm]only thing I seek
To dwell in the [Eb]house of the Lord
For all the [Bb/F]days that I [F]have
{end_of_chorus}

{comment: Outro (instrumental)}
